{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghmP8JmvB9CLopoKMvGp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VzvdgKwxFKZ79EXh3mM5ou","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"this.held = \\|this\\.held=\" my-3d2dge.js | head -3; cat > CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes for OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast\n\nAll in `my-3d2dge.js` (v0.85.2, commit 4390a98), each marked `OutBloom E#` in the source.\n\n| # | Change | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| E3 | `input.analog(action)` (0..1 from the pad's button values, 1 for a held key) and `input.setAnalog(action, v)`; `input.padValues` | Throttle and brake on R2/L2 must be progressive; the engine read pad buttons as on/off only. |\n| E4 | While `AIHub.active`, Options (Pad9) is ignored while Create (Pad8) is held | The hub protocol reserves Create + Options for its corner bar. |\n| E5 | The `glyphs` setting defaults to PlayStation, with Xbox as the only other choice | TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs by default, a Settings option for Xbox. |\n| E6 | Music tokens take chords (`C4+E4+G4`) and accents (`C4!`); tracks take `decay` (plucked notes), `detune` (a unison voice), `lowpass`, `attack`; drum tokens `p` clap, `r` rim, `g` conga, `b` cowbell, `z` shaker, `m` timbale, `y` ride | Latin fusion, city pop and Eurobeat need chords, plucks and percussion that bare chip voices can't carry. |\n| E7 | `audio.loop(spec)`: continuous oscillators and noise with `set()` and `stop()`, silent while paused | A car needs a living engine note, tyre squeal and wind; the engine only had one-shot sounds. |\nEOF","description":"Check held type and write CHANGES.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5051,"cache_read_input_tokens":209989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5051},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b31a73a4-a38b-4945-9f7b-620b7871a8e6","uuid":"161ec632-ca3c-4edf-93df-f68fe87e5abb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:55:48.112Z","request_id":"req_011CghmP81ArxzKPdBAKdGpe","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VzvdgKwxFKZ79EXh3mM5ou":{"command":"grep -n \"this.held = \\|this\\.held=\" my-3d2dge.js | head -3; cat > CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes for OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast\n\nAll in `my-3d2dge.js` (v0.85.2, commit 4390a98), each marked `OutBloom E#` in the source.\n\n| # | Change | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| E3 | `input.analog(action)` (0..1 from the pad's button values, 1 for a held key) and `input.setAnalog(action, v)`; `input.padValues` | Throttle and brake on R2/L2 must be progressive; the engine read pad buttons as on/off only. |\n| E4 | While `AIHub.active`, Options (Pad9) is ignored while Create (Pad8) is held | The hub protocol reserves Create + Options for its corner bar. |\n| E5 | The `glyphs` setting defaults to PlayStation, with Xbox as the only other choice | TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs by default, a Settings option for Xbox. |\n| E6 | Music tokens take chords (`C4+E4+G4`) and accents (`C4!`); tracks take `decay` (plucked notes), `detune` (a unison voice), `lowpass`, `attack`; drum tokens `p` clap, `r` rim, `g` conga, `b` cowbell, `z` shaker, `m` timbale, `y` ride | Latin fusion, city pop and Eurobeat need chords, plucks and percussion that bare chip voices can't carry. |\n| E7 | `audio.loop(spec)`: continuous oscillators and noise with `set()` and `stop()`, silent while paused | A car needs a living engine note, tyre squeal and wind; the engine only had one-shot sounds. |\nEOF","description":"Check held type and write CHANGES.md"}}}
