{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013LyYrABCRKJk8yT9dedDkN","type":"tool_result","content":"// my-3D2dge game checker: loads a game in a headless browser, presses start, plays it for a\n// moment, switches through the game's camera views, and reports errors, warnings, frame rate,\n// how much of the window the picture covers (covers: 1 = no black bars), how much is actually on screen, and screenshots.\n//\n// Setup (once):   npm install          (installs Playwright)\n//                 npx playwright install chromium\n// Usage:          node tools/check.mjs path/to/game.html[#scene] [--seconds 4] [--out check-output] [--size 390x844@3]\n//                 (--size: the window in CSS pixels and its pixel density; @2 and up is a phone or tablet, with touch)\n// Exit code is 1 if the page threw any error or never drew anything, so agents and CI can rely on it.\n// A game that sets game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} } } gets its snapshot printed after play (its own state:\n// the hero, the objective, what an agent needs to see the game is where it should be).\n// a #hash after the file name is kept, so deep links like game.html#platformer work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b31a73a4-a38b-4945-9f7b-620b7871a8e6","uuid":"bae1d3d1-d0dc-42ca-8b74-fa0cc53c3d5e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:44:49.509Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// my-3D2dge game checker: loads a game in a headless browser, presses start, plays it for a\n// moment, switches through the game's camera views, and reports errors, warnings, frame rate,\n// how much of the window the picture covers (covers: 1 = no black bars), how much is actually on screen, and screenshots.\n//\n// Setup (once):   npm install          (installs Playwright)\n//                 npx playwright install chromium\n// Usage:          node tools/check.mjs path/to/game.html[#scene] [--seconds 4] [--out check-output] [--size 390x844@3]\n//                 (--size: the window in CSS pixels and its pixel density; @2 and up is a phone or tablet, with touch)\n// Exit code is 1 if the page threw any error or never drew anything, so agents and CI can rely on it.\n// A game that sets game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} } } gets its snapshot printed after play (its own state:\n// the hero, the objective, what an agent needs to see the game is where it should be).\n// a #hash after the file name is kept, so deep links like game.html#platformer work","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013LyYrABCRKJk8yT9dedDkN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
