{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrTEEf1eYpFHszsT5RR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012hVYGrqy4YVsXigLog6sbk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/01-data-about.js'; s=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\nimport re\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:60]; s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"with five engine changes (analog triggers, hub combo guard, PlayStation glyph default, richer chip synth, continuous sound loops);\", \"with six engine changes (analog triggers, the hub's Create + Options guard, a PlayStation glyph default, a richer chip synth, continuous sound loops, a 10-foot theme for the standard screens);\")\nrep(\"\"\"  testingFeedback: [\n    'unknown',\n    'unknown',\n    'unknown',\n    'unknown'\n  ],\n  engineFeedback: [\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\n  ],\n  promptFeedback: [\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\n  ],\"\"\", \"\"\"  testingFeedback: [\n    'About 25 real issues, plus a few mistakes in my own test setups. Scripts caught the bot steering the wrong way in drifts, rear-ending traffic and running out of time on every route, a drift that counter-steering could not end, two crashes in rival missions, request objects spaced too tightly for anyone to reach, a slider value off by floating point, and a hub message guard. Screenshots caught missing font glyphs, a windscreen drawn over the people, overblown night glows, oversized banners, cars filling the split screen, ending props hiding the characters and crash cushions in the middle of the road.',\n    'Three: every rival mission stopped with a TypeError at the first fork or at the finish (rivals had no fork-warning or split records), and every song lost its melody because the bar separators in the melodies were parsed as NaN notes.',\n    'The bot playthrough of all 16 routes to all 5 goals: it exposed the bot\\\\'s traffic handling, set the clock and stage lengths, and is now the regression net for the whole game. The official AI Hub harness run on the bundle was a close second.',\n    'The engine checker\\\\'s camera-view sweep (iso, three-quarter, top-down, brawler screenshots), which means nothing for a pseudo-3D road racer, and its look notes taken from a frame mid-transition.'\n  ],\n  engineFeedback: [\n    'Exact fixed-step headless play: game.advance with input.tap and hold drove the whole game (menus, races, attract mode, hub sessions) in Node with no browser, deterministically. The free pause, settings, rebinding and Humanoid rigs with live portraits saved a great deal.',\n    'Yes. The road module draws a single road, so forks meant writing my own renderer. Keyboard drop-in for player two needs a real canvas, so it cannot be tested headless. The pixel font has no middle dot, triangles, ellipsis, tick or shamrock; I only learned that from question marks in screenshots.',\n    'The forking pseudo-3D road: two branches with their own continuations into the next stages, per-side grounds and edges, tunnels and spans, and a seamless switch from one stage to the next. Then the car renderer that builds every car from shaded 3D boxes at any yaw.',\n    'Fitting a custom road into the engine\\\\'s draw model (overlays, split-screen viewports, a Backdrop drawn through a stand-in renderer) while keeping it pixel-crisp, and tuning handling and audio by numbers and screenshots alone.',\n    'Six changes in my-3d2dge.js, each marked OutBloom E#: analog trigger values (input.analog) for progressive throttle and brake; Options ignored while Create is held in a hub session; a PlayStation glyph default with Xbox as the option; chords, accents, plucks, detune, lowpass and Latin percussion in the music synth; audio.loop for continuous engine, tyre and wind sounds; and a game theme, CSS and Help screen for the standard HTML menus so they read at TV distance.',\n    'Make the road module branch: junctions with two continuations, per-side grounds and roadside strips, built in. It is the one structure every OutRun-style game needs and the largest thing I had to build.'\n  ],\n  promptFeedback: [\n    'The definition of done is concrete and testable: one file, a dev mode with sliders and reset, attract mode after 10 seconds, the touch-only notice, PlayStation and Xbox glyphs, AI Hub conformance, and the exit interview. Paired with a detailed plan, it left little to guess.',\n    'The plan\\\\'s scope (15 stages, 14 missions, 45 ending lines, 11 songs) set against a medium-effort run, and the plan\\\\'s file names carrying another run\\\\'s effort and timestamp. \"The mouse clicks things in the world\" is hard to place in a racing game.',\n    'Producing that much content (stages, music, voices, lines, endings) and tuning the feel of driving without hearing the sound or holding a pad.',\n    'Give a priority order for when time runs short, name the browser and hardware the game is judged on, and allow a way to check audio (even an automated loudness or spectrum check).'\n  ],\"\"\")\nrep(\"{ h: 'SOURCE INFORMATION (1/2)',\", \"{ h: 'SOURCE INFORMATION (1/3)',\")\nrep(\"{ h: 'SOURCE INFORMATION (2/2)',\", \"{ h: 'SOURCE INFORMATION (2/3)',\")\nrep(\"research: 'The engine\\\\'s handoff docs (README, API card, index, road kit and module), the AI Hub README and harness; source facts from the plan\\\\'s research notes (Wikipedia and a retrospective, as summarised there); no new web research',\", \"research: 'None beyond the provided material: the engine\\\\'s handoff docs (README, API card, index, road kit and module), the AI Hub README and harness, and the source facts in the plan\\\\'s research notes; no new web research',\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf8').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -i 's/^All in `my-3d2dge.js` (v0.85.2, commit 4390a98), each marked `OutBloom E#` in the source.$/All in `my-3d2dge.js` (v0.85.2, commit 4390a98), each marked `OutBloom E#` in the source. The plan'\"'\"'s E1\\/E2 (road junctions and dressing) were built in the game instead (`src\\/10-road.js`), as a forking renderer of its own./' engine/CHANGES.md && head -4 engine/CHANGES.md && node build.mjs && node -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8')); console.log(Object.keys(j), j.testingFeedback.length, j.engineFeedback.length, j.promptFeedback.length, Object.values(j.sourceInformation).every(v=>v&&v.length))\"","description":"Fill feedback answers, rebuild, validate JSON"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_read_input_tokens":694977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2773},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b31a73a4-a38b-4945-9f7b-620b7871a8e6","uuid":"6d404c37-e0f4-4c46-82ba-3432e4b6dedc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:02:51.992Z","request_id":"req_011CghrTDv4Vm4rh8HUhHh1C","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012hVYGrqy4YVsXigLog6sbk":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/01-data-about.js'; s=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\nimport re\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:60]; s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"with five engine changes (analog triggers, hub combo guard, PlayStation glyph default, richer chip synth, continuous sound loops);\", \"with six engine changes (analog triggers, the hub's Create + Options guard, a PlayStation glyph default, a richer chip synth, continuous sound loops, a 10-foot theme for the standard screens);\")\nrep(\"\"\"  testingFeedback: [\n    'unknown',\n    'unknown',\n    'unknown',\n    'unknown'\n  ],\n  engineFeedback: [\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\n  ],\n  promptFeedback: [\n    'unkno